 edges within 800 units, so the apparent closure is a time-ignoring artefact of a very sparse log, not a genuine closure wave."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Structure vs. timing.** The window holds 2,746 events over 1,609 active nodes (repeat_ratio 0.008) \u2014 extremely sparse (step_01). Each of the 12 target nodes sits in exactly **one** static triangle (step_03), i.e. the \"closure\" structure exists when time is ignored. That is precisely the confounder the task warns about, so I tested whether those triangle edges are *temporally* prompt.\n\n**Triangle 1: 34\u2013452\u2013617** (step_06 shows 452 and 617 have no partners outside this triad). All 6 directed events involving {452, 617} \u2014 i.e. the entire triangle \u2014 fall in disjoint 400-unit buckets at \u224839.8k, 43.8k, 44.6k, 45.0k, 46.2k and 50.2k (step_07). The triangle's edges are spread over ~10,000 time units; even the closest candidate support/closure pair (\u224845.0k \u2192 \u224846.2k) exceeds the 800-unit requirement.\n\n**Triangle 2: 220\u2013306\u20131554** (step_04). Activity of this triad is bimodal: 3 events in 40.6k\u201342.6k, then nothing for ~5,000 units, then events at 47.6k\u201350.6k (step_05). At 400-unit resolution the 306/1554 side occurs at \u224841.8k, then 48.6k, 49.4k, 49.8k (step_08). The supporting edges and the third edge are separated by thousands of units, not \u2264800.\n\n**Conclusion:** the triangles are static artefacts of a sparse log, not a temporal closure wave: no support\u2192closure lag falls inside the 800-unit budget.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_0e3f1856\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"closure_wave\",\n  \"entities\": [15, 34, 38, 54, 99, 118, 127, 144, 220, 222, 233, 237, 306, 452, 617, 1554],\n  \"window\": [39646, 51646],\n  \"confidence\": 0.72,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Every listed node participates in exactly one static triangle, but fine-grained temporal binning shows the triangle edges are separated by thousands of time units (34-452-617 spans ~39.8k-50.2k; 220-306-1554 splits into a 41-42k burst and a 48-50k burst). No closing interaction follows its supporting shared-contact edges within 800 units, so the apparent closure is a time-ignoring artefact of a very sparse log, not a genuine closure wave.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 20772, "total_output_tokens": 7173, "total_tokens": 27945, "total_latency_ms": 96249, "llm_calls": 5, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}